    "problemStatement": "Member and committee websites are not reliably built or kept accessible",
    "problemDescription": "Federal accessibility requirements apply to member and committee websites, but awareness of those requirements varies by office, and staff often lack training or tools to keep a site compliant as it is updated. Constituents who use assistive technology cannot reliably use the site of the office that represents them.",
    "solutionStatement": "Train and tool House offices to maintain accessible websites",
    "solutionDescription": "Promote awareness of website accessibility requirements across member and committee offices and give staff standing training and tools to maintain and update accessible sites, rather than leaving offices to discover requirements only after a complaint. The House sustains the training and tooling as staff and site features turn over.",
