    "problemStatement": "Members and staff have no formal training in bipartisan oversight practice",
    "problemDescription": "Oversight skill is picked up on the job, often on committees where the culture already runs adversarial. Members and staff have no formal, common training in how to conduct oversight that is fact-based and works across party lines, so practice varies by committee and by whoever happens to be assigned.",
    "solutionStatement": "Optional bipartisan oversight training for members and staff",
