    "problemStatement": "Ethics rules discourage staff from referring constituents to outside help",
    "problemDescription": "Caseworkers often know a constituent's problem is better solved by a local nonprofit or service provider than by the office itself, but existing ethics guidance is unclear on when a referral to a named outside organization is permitted. Staff err toward silence or a generic list rather than risk an ethics violation, so constituents lose a useful connection the office could have made.",
    "solutionStatement": "Issue clear ethics guidance on community referrals",
    "solutionDescription": "Have the Committee on Ethics issue updated guidance specifying when and how district offices may direct constituents to named community organizations, resources, and services. Caseworkers get a standing rule to work from instead of a case-by-case judgment call, and offices can build referral lists once the rule is settled.",
    "horizonJustification": "Once issued, the guidance is a standing rule every office can rely on without further action, which is what makes it durable rather than a one-time fix.",
