    "problemStatement": "Constituent communications costs compete with staff salaries in office budgets",
    "problemDescription": "Member offices pay for franked mail, newsletters, and other constituent communications out of the same Members' Representational Allowance that funds staff salaries, so heavier communications needs directly reduce what an office can spend on people. Offices with active communications operations trade staffing capacity for outreach as a result.",
    "solutionStatement": "Shared account for constituent communications costs",
    "solutionDescription": "Remove constituent communications expenses from the Members' Representational Allowance and fund them instead through a separate, shared institutional account. Office budgets are freed to focus on staff salaries and operating costs, while communications spending is tracked and funded centrally.",
    "horizonJustification": "A separate, standing funding account is a permanent change to how the institution budgets, not a one-time transfer.",
