    "problemStatement": "Congressional staff have limited access to health insurance options",
    "problemDescription": "Congressional staff, particularly those in district offices, part-time roles, or lower pay bands, have historically faced narrower health insurance options and eligibility rules than staff in comparable federal or private sector jobs. Gaps in coverage make congressional employment less competitive against other offers.",
    "solutionStatement": "Expand health insurance access for congressional staff",
    "solutionDescription": "Broaden eligibility and options for health insurance coverage across House employment categories, including district and part-time staff. Staff gain benefits closer to what comparable employers offer, and offices compete for talent on more even footing.",
