    "problemStatement": "District office lease costs and terms vary with no central negotiation",
    "problemDescription": "Each House district office negotiates its own commercial lease independently, so rental rates and terms vary widely across offices even in similar markets, and no one in the House brings comparative leverage or market data to individual negotiations. The CAO tracks lease payments but does not actively negotiate on offices' behalf.",
    "solutionStatement": "Centralize district office lease negotiation practices",
