    "problemStatement": "Committees lack bipartisan telework policies",
    "problemDescription": "Individual committees set telework arrangements for their staff without a shared, bipartisan process, so policies vary by committee and can shift with a change in chairmanship. Majority and minority staff on the same committee can end up working under different expectations.",
    "solutionStatement": "Committees establish bipartisan telework policies",
    "solutionDescription": "Have each committee set its telework policy on a bipartisan basis, agreed to by both majority and minority staff. Telework expectations hold steady for committee staff regardless of which party controls the gavel.",
    "horizonJustification": "Each committee still sets its own policy independently, so there is no shared standard or owner ensuring consistency across committees or over time.",
