    "problemStatement": "Local funding priorities bypass congressional appropriators entirely",
    "problemDescription": "For roughly a decade, directed spending was barred from the appropriations process, leaving decisions about which local infrastructure and community projects get funded largely to executive branch formulas and agency discretion rather than the members closest to the need. Congress's Article One power to direct specific spending sat unused, and local investments received little public accounting when other channels funded them instead.",
