    "problemStatement": "The President's budget request offers Congress little useful structure",
    "problemDescription": "The executive branch submits its annual budget request in a format and on a timeline that often arrives late and organized in ways that do not match how congressional appropriators actually build bills. Committees end up reconciling the executive's categories with their own before substantive budget work can start.",
